\figref{fig:walk-orders} contrasts the two orders that matter. The tree is
the same in both pictures; the number under each node is the position of
that node in the visit sequence. A pre-order walk reaches a node before
its children, which is what a printer wants: the tag is known before the
subtree is written. A post-order walk reaches a node after its children,
which is what a folder wants: the children have already been reduced when
the parent is examined.

